| **Data Minimization** (Art. 5(1)(c)) | **A01: Broken Access Control** | Users can access data they shouldn't (e.g., viewing other users' medical records). |
| **Security of Processing** (Art. 32) | **A02: Cryptographic Failures** | Sensitive data (passwords, health info) is stored/transmitted in plain text. |
| **Accountability** (Art. 5(2)) | **A05: Security Misconfiguration** | Lack of logging/audit trails makes it impossible to prove compliance or investigate breaches. |

